## Plan Handoff Contract

- **Accepted planning sources:** {{HANDOFF_SOURCES}}.
- **Canonical required fields (12):** Task; Source plan; Owned paths; Read-only paths; Relevant gates; Constraints; Dependencies / wave; Required approvals; Runtime format target; Expected output; Context freshness; Lossiness.
- **Expansion fields:** Owning agent, Evidence, and task-specific expansion blocks are included only when useful; they are not part of the required minimum.
- **Triage seed:** requirements-triage may prefill intent, scope, risks, questions, and routing, but the orchestrator must validate it before delegation.
- **Prompt assignment quality:** normal/risky work uses a structured subtask slice; safe tiny work may use short-form and report `warn` for non-blocking gaps.
- **Context packet rule:** pass task-specific files, facts, decisions, and references; do not paste full project memory, full plans, or unrelated logs into every subagent prompt.
- **Capabilities and skills:** describe allowed capabilities and skills referenced; never invent skill names or ask agents to mutate their own runtime frontmatter/TOML.
- **Assignment marker:** `Task assignment quality: ok | warn | fail; form=<short|full>; missing=<fields|none>; questions=<count>`.
- **Format rule:** generated artifacts must use the selected runtime's native schema; never copy prompt frontmatter or another runtime's frontmatter into this project.
- **Platform format targets:** {{PLATFORM_FORMAT_NOTES}}
- **Handoff evidence:** {{HANDOFF_EVIDENCE}}

### Platform-native delegation

| Runtime | Delegation surface | Note |
|---|---|---|
| Copilot CLI / VS Code | Task/custom-agent calls through the orchestrator's `agent` capability | Use Task/agent fan-out for synthesized work; `/fleet` is optional CLI UX for independent batches. |
| Claude Code | `Agent` tool | Fan out independent subagents in one wave; Agent Teams remain opt-in/experimental. |
| OpenCode | `task` / `@<agent-name>` from a primary agent | Gate delegation with `permission.task` wildcard deny/ask plus named roster allows. |
| OpenAI Codex (CLI + App) | Root `AGENTS.md` asks Codex to spawn child agents; specialists live in `.codex/agents/*.toml` | Keep shared artifacts free of required CLI-only slash commands. |
| Gemini CLI | Root `GEMINI.md` session delegates to `.gemini/agents/*.md` local subagents | Gemini subagents cannot recursively delegate; root session owns all fan-out. |

